message: "If you use this code or the recovered per-episode perturbation labels, please cite the following."
title: "SmolVLA_RL: Low-Budget Flow-SDE GRPO Fine-Tuning of a Flow-Matching VLA"
authors:
  - family-names: Ono
    given-names: Katsuki
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ono-Katsuki/SmolVLA_RL"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-23"
keywords:
  - vision-language-action
  - reinforcement-learning
  - flow-matching
  - GRPO
  - LIBERO
  - robot-learning
abstract: >-
  A single-GPU, single-suite proof of concept for online RL fine-tuning of the
  flow-matching VLA SmolVLA using a Flow-SDE GRPO objective on LIBERO-Plus. The
  repository documents two silent gradient pathologies (element-count ratio
  normalization and chunk-weighting bias), a staged privileged reward with a
  diagnostic funnel, and a fully scripted Colab pipeline.
